  obs doctor mcp-interpreter check + --json fix (2026-08-17, PRs #96/#97, merged to dev): fixed
  the Claude Desktop MCP outage this session — a Homebrew python@3.14 patch bump (3.14.6→3.14.7)
  deleted a version-pinned Cellar path the obsidian-ops MCP entry was hardcoded to, and `obs
  doctor` reported all-pass throughout. Added `mcp-interpreter` to the `mcp` layer: fails on a
  dead/non-executable/unresolvable interpreter, warns when it resolves but is pinned to a
  version-specific Homebrew Cellar path (incl. revision-suffixed, e.g. `3.14.6_1`) — the exact
  fragility that broke. Adversarial review (opencode) caught a crash bug (non-string `command`
  value raised an uncaught TypeError) and the revision-suffix regex gap before merge; both fixed
  with regression tests. Also fixed a separate pre-existing bug found along the way: `obs doctor
  --json` crashed on every layer (`UnboundLocalError` from a shadowed local `import json`
  elsewhere in `obs_cli.py`'s `main()`), spun off as PR #97. Added e2e (real subprocess,
  `E2E=1`-gated) + dogfood (in-process via `obs_cli.main()`) coverage for both. Tests: 603 pytest
  (non-e2e) + 138 e2e collected.
